# Fullhan boot header, from Flash_FH8856_NORFLASH_DDR_792MHZ.img
# root: the first 0x100 bytes as they are; the record counts
# and header size are recomputed
# FH885x V100 (FH8852/FH8856): the boot header of the SDK's NOR image
# (FH8856_IPC_V1.2.0, Flash_FH8856_NORFLASH_DDR_792MHZ.img; its FH8852
# image has the same). The ROM starts the SDK's ramboot
# (RamBoot_FH8856_FH8852.bin, fh885xv100.ramboot), which runs the DDR
# script of the package -- 1 Gbit for the FH8856, 512 Mbit for the FH8852
# -- and loads the type-0x11 U-Boot from where this header says (the same
# ramboot loads it from 0x50000 in the SDK's NOR images, 0x60000 in its
# NAND ones). FH8852 cameras seen in the field have the ROM load U-Boot
# directly instead, with the 512 Mbit script alone.
